the centenario stadium in montevideo  hosted the first ever world cup final in  1930 with hosts uruguay becoming the  first world champions  now uruguay is teaming up with argentina  paraguay and chile to host the 2030  world cup so that 100 years on they can  bring the tournament home  it will be the jubilee the celebration  of 100 years in the place where it all  began where they had the guts the  bravery the courage the intelligence and  the effort to start things up  the unprecedented four country bid is  called juntos 2030 which means together  2030.  all of the countries except paraguay  have previously hosted the tournament  individually  they've been working for more than three  years to get this bid off the ground  alongside south america's football  governing body comma bowl  with this joint bid marking a hundred  years we believe that it is very  important and deserving that the world  recognizes that south america has  contributed and continues to contribute  to world football  if successful the tournament could not  be more different to the one held a  century ago  in 1930 there were only 13 teams and the  whole thing was played in the same city  in just three stadiums  in 2030 there will be 48 teams with  around 15 stadiums used across the four  countries fifa expect a decision on the  hosting rights within two years but  there will be competition  romania greece bulgaria and serbia are  also lining up a four country bid  there's a joint bid from spain and  portugal and morocco is trying to become  the second african country to host  the tournament is still eight years away  though while qatar 2022 the first world  cup in the middle east is now just 110  days away and then it'll be the turn of  the us canada and mexico to host in 2026  the biggest world cup to date with 48  teams held across three countries david  stokes al jazeera
 

